false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-12-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IL"},{"bioguideId":"C001119","fullName":"Rep. Craig, Angie [D-MN-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-01-16","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MN"},{"bioguideId":"G000599","fullName":"Rep. Goldman, Daniel S. [D-NY-10]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-03-03","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NY"},{"bioguideId":"D000617","fullName":"Rep. DelBene, Suzan K. [D-WA-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-03-24","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"WA"},{"bioguideId":"M001232","fullName":"Rep. McClain Delaney, April [D-MD-6]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-04-22","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MD"},{"bioguideId":"M001246","fullName":"Rep. Mejia, Analilia [D-NJ-11]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-06-03","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NJ"},{"bioguideId":"G000606","fullName":"Rep. Grijalva, Adelita S. [D-AZ-7]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-08-31","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"AZ"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-20T14:13:10+00:00","id":"hr2021-119","introducedDate":"2025-03-10","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-03-10","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Education and Workforce."},"laws":[],"number":"2021","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Education","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"W000808","district":24,"fullName":"Rep. Wilson, Frederica S. [D-FL-24]","party":"D","state":"FL"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-03-10","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>American Teacher Act</strong></p><p>This bill establishes grants to increase the minimum salary of public elementary and secondary school teachers. It also authorizes a national campaign regarding the value of the teaching profession.</p><p>First, the bill directs the Department of Education (ED) to award four-year grants to state educational agencies (SEAs)&nbsp;and, through them, subgrants to local educational agencies to establish a minimum annual salary of $60,000 (to be adjusted annually for inflation) for these teachers.</p><p>Second, the bill directs ED to award grants to eligible SEAs&nbsp;to provide cost-of-living adjustments to the annual base salary of teachers.</p><p>Finally, the bill authorizes ED to carry out a national campaign to (1) increase awareness about the importance of teachers and the value of the teaching profession, (2) encourage secondary school and college students to consider teaching as a professional career, and (3) diversify the pool of individuals who enter the teaching profession.</p>","updateDate":"2025-05-14T19:58:14Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"American Teacher Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-19T23:20:14Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-19T23:20:14Z"}
